WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.980
The Boeing company proposes a
personal transportation system,

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.280
or PTS, which provides point
to point transportation

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.440
for individuals using
a number of taxi

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.170
like personal aerial vehicles.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:18.350
Our goal in model based
embedded in robotic systems

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.020
is to have humans and
robots collaborate together

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.470
to achieve high level goals
defined by human operators.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.290
We demonstrate the capability
of our architecture

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.290
on a personal transportation
system scenario,

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.509
where the personal
aerial vehicle takes off

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:35.360
from Provincetown
and heads to Bedford.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.600
On the way, there are
multiple nearby airports,

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.360
and each airport has a no fly
zone that must be avoided.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.020
The user inputs the
trip specification

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.290
by highlighting start
goal, alternative landing

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.910
sites, and no fly zones using
the graphical user interface.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.960
The pike module calculates the
corresponding visibility graph

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.960
and the shortest path from
the start to the goal.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.120
If the remaining fuel
capacity is not sufficient,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.500
pike generates the path to the
closest alternative landing

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.370
site.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.440
The generated path
is communicated

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.550
to Sulu and the users through
the graphical interface.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.040
Here, the GUI updates
the real time location

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.790
of the plane while in the corner
is a flight simulation using

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:20.990
X-Plane.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:24.860
A personal aerial vehicle takes
off from Provincetown Municipal

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:25.910
Airport.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.790
The architecture automatically
navigates the vehicle

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.400
to the user specified
destination.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.800
The system is also
capable of adapting

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.720
to a changing environment.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.630
For example, if a storm
approaches the vehicle,

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.920
it will automatically replan
the path to avoid the storm.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.570
Of course, the replanned path
respects all the no fly zones.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.400
The system keeps
updating the plan

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.520
based on the current best
available information.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.680
This demonstration
shows the capabilities

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.890
of our autonomous system in
providing safe and optimal

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.330
paths in a dynamic environment.

